# Recurring Asset Failures → Document Path Forward

When fixing a **repeat** of a known sample-asset failure class (missing player locomotion clips, muddy/glitchy foliage atlases, corrupted Tier-1 prop bakes after import):

## Rules

1. Fix the immediate asset with the named bake / restore path — do not invent a one-off undocumented workaround.
2. Update `context/testing/recurring-asset-failures.md` if the path changed (or add a new section for a new class).
3. Add or extend a `context/testing/findings.md` entry (newest first) with a **Path forward when this recurs** bullet linking that playbook section.
4. Do not leave the next agent to rediscover the same console string or atlas failure from chat history alone.

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD: Rebake player.gltf, move on; next session hits ANIM-CLIP-MISSING again with no playbook
✅ GOOD: Rebake + confirm clip names; findings entry + recurring-asset-failures Player section current

❌ BAD: Tweak bush_tall.png by hand only and forget the baker flag that caused muddy camo
✅ GOOD: Fix PROPS / bake; document Fix now + Prevent in recurring-asset-failures
```
